nts would be 3 (A) +1 (C) +3 (D) +1 (E) = 8. Then A has 7, which is less than B's 8. That violates the condition that A is the top scorer. Therefore, B cannot have more than 6 points if A is to have more. Therefore, the previous scenario where B has 6, A has 7 is the only way.\n\nBut let's verify again. Let me list all the matches with results:\n\n1. A vs B: B wins \u2192 B:3, A:0\n\n2. A vs C: Draw \u2192 A:1, C:1\n\n3. A vs D: A wins \u2192 A:3, D:0\n\n4. A vs E: A wins \u2192 A:3, E:0\n\n5. B vs C: Draw \u2192 B:1, C:1\n\n6. B vs D: Draw \u2192 B:1, D:1\n\n7. B vs E: Draw \u2192 B:1, E:1\n\n8. C vs D: Draw \u2192 C:1, D:1\n\n9. C vs E: Draw \u2192 C:1, E:1\n\n10. D vs E: D wins \u2192 D:3, E:0\n\nNow, let's calculate each team's points:\n\n- Team A: 0 (B) +1 (C) +3 (D) +3 (E) = 7\n\n- Team B: 3 (A) +1 (C) +1 (D) +1 (E) = 6\n\n- Team C:1 (A) +1 (B) +1 (D) +1 (E) =4\n\n- Team D:0 (A) +1 (B) +1 (C) +3 (E) =5\n\n- Team E:0 (A) +1 (B) +1 (C) +0 (D) =2\n\nYes, this adds up. Total points:7+6+4+5+2=24. Let's check total matches:10 matches. Each match contributes:\n\n1. 3 points (B win)\n\n2. 2 points (draw)\n\n3. 3 points (A win)\n\n4. 3 points (A win)\n\n5. 2 points (draw)\n\n6. 2 points (draw)\n\n7. 2 points (draw)\n\n8. 2 points (draw)\n\n9. 2 points (draw)\n\n10.3 points (D win)\n\nTotal points:3+2+3+3+2+2+2+2+2+3=24. Yes, correct.\n\nAll conditions are met:\n\n- All teams have different points (7,6,5,4,2).\n\n- A is top with 7, despite losing to B.\n\n- B and C have no losses (B: 1 win, 3 draws; C: 4 draws).\n\n- C (4) < D (5).\n\nThis seems to fit. But wait, Team C has all draws. Is that allowed? Yes, the condition is they didn't lose any games, so all draws are fine.\n\nIs there any other possible configuration? Let's see.\n\nSuppose Team C has a win instead of some draws. For example, if C beats D, then C would get 3 points instead of 1. But then D would lose to C, but D needs to have more points than C. Let's try:\n\nIf C beats D: Match 8: C wins \u2192 C:3, D:0