[\n    S_{\\triangle KMZ} = \\frac{1}{2} MK \\cdot MZ \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)\n    \\]\n\n10. The area of triangle $ABC$:\n    \\[\n    S_{\\triangle ABC} = \\frac{1}{2} AB \\cdot BC \\sin (\\angle ABC) = \\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\alpha}\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\beta}\\right) \\sin (180^\\circ - (\\alpha + \\beta))\n    \\]\n    Using the property of sine: $\\sin (180^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$,\n    \\[\n    S_{\\triangle ABC} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\alpha}\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\beta}\\right) \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)\n    \\]\n\n11. The ratio of $S_{\\triangle KMZ}$ to $S_{\\triangle ABC}$:\n    \\[\n    \\frac{S_{\\triangle KMZ}}{S_{\\triangle ABC}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)}{\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\alpha}\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin \\beta}\\right) \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)}\n    \\]\n    Simplifying, we get:\n    \\[\n    \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)}{\\frac{1}{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta} \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\frac{1}{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}} = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\n    \\]\n\n12. Using the double-angle identities $\\sin 2\\theta = 2 \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$:\n    \\[\n    \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\frac{1}{4} (\\sin 2\\alpha \\sin 2\\beta)\n    \\]\n\n13. Therefore, the ratio of the areas is:\n    \\[\n    \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4} \\sin 2 \\alpha \\sin 2 \\beta}\n    \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In a tournament, each chess player scored half of all their points in matches against participants who took the last three places. How many people participated in the tournament in total?", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out this chess tournament problem. So the quest